00:00:08.435 --> 00:00:10.203
shortly.

00:00:10.337 --> 00:00:12.038
&gt;&gt;&gt; Thousands protesting in

00:00:12.172 --> 00:00:14.608
South Africa last week demanding

00:00:14.741 --> 00:00:16.376
realistic action against the

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:17.577
prolonged energy crisis.

00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:19.045
For months now the country has

00:00:19.179 --> 00:00:21.581
been facing rolling blackouts

00:00:21.581 --> 00:00:22.749
which have crippled the economy

00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:24.918
and paralyzed major cities.

00:00:25.051 --> 00:00:27.154
For let's go to David Mackenzie

00:00:27.587 --> 00:00:29.589
who joins us live from

00:00:29.623 --> 00:00:29.923
johannesburg.

00:00:30.056 --> 00:00:31.725
Actually the problem goes back

00:00:31.858 --> 00:00:32.726
years, doesn't it?

00:00:32.859 --> 00:00:33.593
&gt;&gt; Reporter: That's right.

00:00:33.627 --> 00:00:35.929
It goes back to at least 2007,

00:00:36.062 --> 00:00:36.196
max.

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:37.597
In the last few months you have

00:00:37.664 --> 00:00:39.900
seen the disas Strauss effect of

00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:41.601
lack of planning and general

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:42.435
chaos and corruption at the

00:00:42.569 --> 00:00:44.838
energy utility here in south

00:00:44.971 --> 00:00:45.172
Africa.

00:00:45.605 --> 00:00:47.641
It has a massive impact on the

00:00:47.774 --> 00:00:49.976
economy and just ordinary south

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.611
Africans and have to say some of

00:00:51.611 --> 00:00:55.081
these images may be disturbing.

00:00:55.215 --> 00:00:57.951
Tens of thousands of dead birds.

00:00:58.084 --> 00:01:00.020
Suffocated when the power failed

00:01:00.153 --> 00:01:00.720
and surges blew the backup

00:01:00.854 --> 00:01:02.622
systems.

00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:04.090
It's the awful impact of a

00:01:04.224 --> 00:01:08.328
country in crisis.

00:01:08.461 --> 00:01:09.930
When you saw thousands of

00:01:10.063 --> 00:01:11.898
chickens die like this, what was

00:01:12.032 --> 00:01:14.100
it like for you?

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:15.969
&gt;&gt; Glass of cold water in your

00:01:16.102 --> 00:01:16.469
face.

00:01:16.603 --> 00:01:23.143
It was so, so bad.

00:01:23.276 --> 00:01:24.678
&gt;&gt; Reporter: He has struggled

00:01:24.811 --> 00:01:26.479
with up to ten hours of rolling

00:01:26.613 --> 00:01:27.647
blackouts a day.

00:01:27.647 --> 00:01:31.051
He can't hide his anger at the

00:01:31.184 --> 00:01:31.651
government.

00:01:31.651 --> 00:01:32.752
&gt;&gt; I'm not asking them to do me

00:01:32.886 --> 00:01:33.987
a favor.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.089
I I will do my job and produce

00:01:36.223 --> 00:01:37.858
food and wake up early, work on

00:01:37.991 --> 00:01:39.326
Sundays to produce food for

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:39.826
South Africa.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.328
I like what I'm doing.

00:01:41.661 --> 00:01:43.864
Just do your job.

00:01:43.997 --> 00:01:45.665
You have one thing to do, just

00:01:45.665 --> 00:01:45.932
do it.

00:01:46.066 --> 00:01:48.268
Just give us power, please.

00:01:48.401 --> 00:01:49.669
&gt;&gt; Reporter: But power is in

00:01:49.703 --> 00:01:51.004
short supply.

00:01:51.137 --> 00:01:52.439
The farm they built from scratch

00:01:52.572 --> 00:01:54.708
now runs at a loss during the

00:01:54.841 --> 00:01:57.210
worst blackouts.

00:01:57.344 --> 00:01:58.211
He says diesel costs could sink

00:01:58.345 --> 00:01:59.746
them.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.983
The president himself has

00:02:03.116 --> 00:02:04.751
admitted corruption, sabotage, a

00:02:04.885 --> 00:02:07.220
lack of skills has caused this

00:02:07.354 --> 00:02:08.722
issue.

00:02:08.855 --> 00:02:10.490
Why should this government be

00:02:10.624 --> 00:02:11.691
trusted to fix it.

00:02:11.691 --> 00:02:13.827
&gt;&gt; David, as you know this

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:14.694
predates the president's time in

00:02:14.828 --> 00:02:16.763
government.

00:02:16.897 --> 00:02:17.831
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Even the president

00:02:17.964 --> 00:02:20.667
now acknowledges that decades of

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.769
mismanagement and breathtaking

00:02:22.903 --> 00:02:26.606
corruption crippled state owned

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.008
escom, a lack of maintenance, a

00:02:28.141 --> 00:02:31.711
deep skills deficit an

00:02:31.745 --> 00:02:33.079
regulatory red tape has helped

00:02:33.213 --> 00:02:33.713
cause this.

00:02:33.713 --> 00:02:34.881
&gt;&gt; I will repeat the same

00:02:35.015 --> 00:02:36.850
question which is why should

00:02:36.983 --> 00:02:37.918
south Africans trust the

00:02:38.051 --> 00:02:39.019
government that caused this

00:02:39.152 --> 00:02:40.787
problem to fix this problem?

00:02:40.921 --> 00:02:44.291
&gt;&gt; We accept those mistakes.

00:02:44.424 --> 00:02:45.992
I've said it and the president

00:02:46.126 --> 00:02:48.194
has said it numerous times there

00:02:48.328 --> 00:02:51.164
were massive regrettable policy

00:02:51.298 --> 00:02:52.232
missteps that led us to where we

00:02:52.365 --> 00:02:54.534
are now, however, now we're

00:02:54.668 --> 00:02:56.169
focusing on the solution and the

00:02:56.303 --> 00:02:56.870
opportunities that have been

00:02:57.003 --> 00:03:02.709
presented by this crisis.

00:03:02.842 --> 00:03:03.777
&gt;&gt; For energy security.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:04.477
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Not everyone is

00:03:04.611 --> 00:03:05.745
buying it.

00:03:05.745 --> 00:03:06.513
The official opposition is

00:03:06.646 --> 00:03:08.915
calling for mass action.

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:10.750
You can sense the growing

00:03:10.884 --> 00:03:12.319
frustration in South Africa

00:03:12.452 --> 00:03:12.652
already.

00:03:12.786 --> 00:03:14.955
This crisis isn't just

00:03:15.088 --> 00:03:17.757
inconvenient for people, it can

00:03:17.757 --> 00:03:19.759
kill the dreams of a better

00:03:19.759 --> 00:03:19.859
future.

00:03:19.993 --> 00:03:23.763
A better future is what this

00:03:23.763 --> 00:03:24.364
family strives for.

00:03:24.497 --> 00:03:25.432
Are you proud of yourself?

00:03:25.765 --> 00:03:28.168
&gt;&gt; Yes, I am.

00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:29.836
But we used to fight a lot.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.272
&gt;&gt; Okay, that's caramel.

00:03:32.405 --> 00:03:34.174
&gt;&gt; Reporter: He turned a small

00:03:34.307 --> 00:03:36.109
government covid grant into the

00:03:36.242 --> 00:03:38.511
soweto creamery.

00:03:38.645 --> 00:03:40.180
It's a huge hit here thanks to

00:03:40.313 --> 00:03:42.415
the whole family.

00:03:42.549 --> 00:03:43.984
But when the power goes out,

00:03:44.117 --> 00:03:46.853
their profits evaporate.

00:03:46.987 --> 00:03:51.057
&gt;&gt; So now about to turn on the

00:03:51.191 --> 00:03:51.458
generator.

00:03:51.791 --> 00:03:52.125
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Their plans to

00:03:52.258 --> 00:03:55.929
expand put on hold.

00:03:56.062 --> 00:03:57.030
What do you want the government

00:03:57.163 --> 00:03:57.797
to do?

00:03:57.797 --> 00:04:01.801
&gt;&gt; I want the government to be

00:04:01.935 --> 00:04:02.736
brutally honest with us.

00:04:02.869 --> 00:04:04.637
If they're able to fix it,

00:04:04.771 --> 00:04:05.338
please fix it.

00:04:05.472 --> 00:04:07.474
If they can't they must let us

00:04:07.807 --> 00:04:09.009
know and makes us feel we are

00:04:09.142 --> 00:04:13.179
not really in a democracy

00:04:13.313 --> 00:04:15.815
because it's meant for the

00:04:15.949 --> 00:04:19.019
people by the people but it's as

00:04:19.152 --> 00:04:21.054
if for them by them.

00:04:21.187 --> 00:04:22.389
&gt;&gt; Reporter: At the very least

00:04:22.522 --> 00:04:24.424
he and all south Africans just

00:04:24.557 --> 00:04:25.325
want the lights to be turned

00:04:25.458 --> 00:04:28.328
back on.

00:04:28.461 --> 00:04:30.964
You really can feel the

00:04:31.097 --> 00:04:33.500
frustration of millions of south

00:04:33.833 --> 00:04:34.934
Africans, max, who feel they are

00:04:35.068 --> 00:04:38.104
not being met with the support.

00:04:38.238 --> 00:04:39.472
In some cases just to get

00:04:39.839 --> 00:04:40.707
themselves out of poverty or

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.442
feed the nation and this has

00:04:42.575 --> 00:04:44.110
broader implications.

00:04:44.244 --> 00:04:45.211
Protests, you mentioned.

00:04:45.345 --> 00:04:47.914
More have been planned for later

00:04:48.048 --> 00:04:50.183
in February and in March.

00:04:50.316 --> 00:04:51.451
It threatens the stability of

